'' A procedure named as a type in a unit that DECLARES A GENERIC is still fbc's error 14
'' (fbc-modern 1.20, 2026-11-03). Such a unit is walked twice -- a discovery pass whose
'' diagnostics are rolled back, then the real one -- and TKO0997 was kept to one report per
'' node by the ref the first pass set, so the real pass said nothing and 'dim a as F'
'' compiled. Reported exactly once.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -c tests/diagnostics/src/proc-as-type-generic.bas -o tests/diagnostics/src/proc-as-type-generic.o
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: proc-as-type-generic.bas(7,10): error TKO0997: 'f' is a procedure, not a type
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0808
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 1
